{"name":"Teddy Bear","hex":"#9d8164","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Teddy Bear","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A British Rail Class 14 locomotive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Teddy_Bear"}],"entries":[{"title":"Teddy bear","blocks":[{"text":"A teddy bear, or simply a teddy, is a stuffed toy in the form of a bear. The teddy bear was named by Morris Michtom after the 26th president of the United States, Theodore Roosevelt; it was developed apparently simultaneously in the first decade of the 20th century by two toymakers: Richard Steiff in Germany and Michtom in the United States. It became a popular children's toy, and it has been celebrated in story, song, and film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Teddy_bear_early_1900s_-_Smithsonian_Museum_of_Natural_History.jpg/330px-Teddy_bear_early_1900s_-_Smithsonian_Museum_of_Natural_History.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teddy_bear","wikidata":"Q213477"},{"title":"Teddy Bear (STAYC song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Teddy Bear\" is a song recorded by South Korean girl group STAYC for their fourth single album of the same name. It was released as the single album's lead single by High Up Entertainment on February 14, 2023."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teddy_Bear_(STAYC_song)","wikidata":"Q116827849"},{"title":"Teddy","blocks":[{"text":"Teddy is an English language given name, usually a hypocorism of Edward or Theodore or Theodora. It may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teddy","wikidata":"Q18010041"},{"title":"Bear","blocks":[{"text":"Bears are carnivoran mammals of the family Ursidae. They are classified as caniforms within the suborder Caniformia. Although only eight species of bears are extant, they are widespread, appearing in a wide variety of habitats throughout most of the Northern Hemisphere and partially in the Southern Hemisphere. Bears are found on the continents of North America, South America, and Eurasia. Common characteristics of modern bears include large bodies with stocky legs, long snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hair, plantigrade paws with five nonretractile claws, and short tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg/330px-Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear","wikidata":"Q11788"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg/500px-Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg/500px-Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/TheodoreRooseveltTeddyBear.jpg/500px-TheodoreRooseveltTeddyBear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/TheodoreRooseveltTeddyBear.jpg/500px-TheodoreRooseveltTeddyBear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1902 political cartoon in The Washington Post  spawned the teddy bear name.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATheodoreRooseveltTeddyBear.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/RPPC_%22Merry_Christmas_to_Gardiner_from%27Teddy%27%22.jpg/500px-RPPC_%22Merry_Christmas_to_Gardiner_from%27Teddy%27%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed